ngle, background, and lighting.\n<Audio 1>: fully_copy - the complete source signal is copied 1:1 and used as the target video's sole final audio track, preserving its original duration, timing, vocals, guitar performance, pauses, breathing, room tone, loudness, and all existing audible details.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video uses a photorealistic, intimate live-performance style with natural facial animation, physically accurate guitar playing, stable character identity, and consistent scene details. It is presented as one uninterrupted shot.\n\n[Shot 1] The video begins exactly from <Picture 1>. <Subject 1> (S1) and <Subject 2> remain in the precise opening pose, position, scale, orientation, and framing established by the first frame. Preserve the woman's face, hairstyle, clothing, accessories, body proportions, and posture. Preserve the guitar's shape, color, material, fretboard, strings, orientation, and contact with her body. The original background, lighting direction, shadows, depth of field, and color balance remain visually consistent throughout the shot.\n\nAs <Audio 1> begins, <Subject 1> (S1) naturally starts playing the guitar and physically singing the exact vocal content already present in the reused audio. Her lips, jaw, cheeks, and throat move in precise synchronization with the original syllables, sustained notes, phrasing, rhythm, emotional delivery, breaths, and pauses. Her mouth remains naturally relaxed whenever the vocal layer is silent.\n\nHer guitar performance follows <Audio 1> accurately. The strumming or picking hand moves in time with every audible stroke and rhythmic accent, while the fretboard hand forms plausible chord shapes and changes position naturally according to the harmonic progression. Finger motion remains anatomically correct and temporally stable. The hands maintain believable contact with the strings, neck, and body of the guitar without drifting or changing shape.\n\nThe woman's upper body responds subtly to the performance through gentle breathing, small shoulder movement, restrained head motion, occasional natural blinking, slight changes in eye direction, and expressive but controlled facial reactions. Her emotion follows the intensity and phrasing of the singing without exaggerated gestures. Her identity, facial geometry, hands, guitar, clothing, and background remain consistent throughout the complete video.\n\nThe camera maintains the composition established by <Picture 1> while shaking slightly with very small amplitude at slow speed, resembling restrained handheld breathing from a nearby camera operator. The movement is smooth, irregular, and subtle rather than rhythmic. The camera does not change its focal length or substantially alter the framing.\n\nThe performance continues for the full duration of <Audio 1>. The final mouth movement, guitar stroke, and hand motion finish precisely with the corresponding final sounds. The woman then settles naturally while the final frame remains stable.\n\noverall_soundscape:\n<Audio 1> is directly reused as the sole and complete final audio track. The audible singing, guitar performance, breathing, room tone, and all other existing sound details remain exactly synchronized with the visible performance.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A",
